    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0578" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.85/10–1747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-17T18:00:00-05:00">October 17, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>711. Embassy today received Foreign Office reply dated October 15<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d517-f1"/> to Embassy note 596 [<hi rendition="#italic">598</hi>] of
                    August 27 Embassy despatch No. 31 October 10<anchor n="12" xml:id="d517-f2"/>
                    concerning discriminations against American shipping. With reference to Law 10
                    of 1946, Foreign Office points out foreign companies have access to Colombian
                    courts and Council of State. With reference to discrimination by Coffee
                    Federation, Foreign Office maintains latter is private entity. It also reminds
                    Embassy that by virtue of Public Resolution 17 passed by 73rd Congress<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d517-f3"/> exportation of American products obtained through
                    loans made by official entities must be exported exclusively in ships of
                    American registry.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d517-f1" n="11" xml:id="d517-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it was transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in his
                    despatch 49, October 21, 1947.</p>
            </note>
